  "reason": "Evidence: The best multimodal config (config_048: multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.525, while the best rna_only config (config_008: multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) achieves 0.530. This suggests the image modality with ResNet50 has not yet provided a clear advantage over RNA alone. The most important open question is whether a stronger image encoder (ImageNet ViT-L) can make the multimodal model outperform the RNA-only baseline. config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) differs from config_048 only in the image encoder, making it a clean single-variable comparison. If it outperforms both config_048 and config_008, it confirms that image information is valuable but was underexploited by ResNet50; if it does not, it strongly supports that the image modality is not contributing meaningfully in this task, redirecting effort toward RNA encoder or aggregation choices. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it resolves the central question of whether multimodality is worth pursuing."
}

